Subject: [PATCH] first_boot: run SetupEnvironment and wait for volumes before FirstBootPrompt

FirstBootPrompt's language list looked empty on a fresh live boot.
Traced with an instrumented build (write the trace to a file, since
stderr from a launch_daemon job never reaches serial.log or syslog):
BLocaleRoster::GetAvailableCatalogs() actually succeeds and the list
view really does get populated (66 items, i.e. one entry per catalog
language twice over -- consistent with both the plaintext add-on and
the embedded default catalog answering) -- so the catalog scan was
never the problem. Every single item's label was simply the empty
string: BLanguage::GetNativeName() returned "" for every language,
while the exact same call via the Locale preflet after reaching the
desktop returns correct native names for all of them.

The difference is environment, not code. data/launch/user's `desktop`
target (and the standalone app_server service) both start with
`env /system/boot/SetupEnvironment`, which is also where the LC_*
locale environment variables (LC_MESSAGES, LC_CTYPE, ...) get
exported -- ICU's default locale and its display-name tables are
driven by exactly those variables. `first_boot`'s job had no such env
line, so FirstBootPrompt launched with none of that set, and ICU fell
back to a state where getDisplayName() comes back empty. By the time
anything in a normal desktop session asks the same question, it's
running under the `desktop` target and inherits the properly set up
environment.

Give `first_boot` the same `env /system/boot/SetupEnvironment` line
the `desktop` target already has, and (kept from the first attempt at
this) gate the job on `on initial_volumes_mounted` like the desktop
target's own services, so it doesn't start before volumes are mounted
either.

diff --git a/data/launch/user b/data/launch/user
index d15a4d19e3..b0ef560292 100644
--- a/data/launch/user
+++ b/data/launch/user
@@ -63,7 +63,11 @@ target desktop {
 }

 target first_boot {
-	job x-vnd.Haiku-FirstBootPrompt
+	env /system/boot/SetupEnvironment
+
+	job x-vnd.Haiku-FirstBootPrompt {
+		on initial_volumes_mounted
+	}
 }

 target installer {
